0$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{1}{4}}\\cos{\\left(2 \\pi x \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x &= {\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}1\\cos(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2 \\pi}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\cos(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}}{2 \\pi}\\big|_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{2 \\pi}-(0) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{2 \\pi}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482722 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186482712 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482722 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482722 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{27}}\\sin{\\left(9 x + \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482722 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d6b42e8b-fdca-50f0-be23-a0ae2f737155" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482722 #edb/ref 1074 "If we let $u=9 x + \\frac{\\pi}{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=9\\,\\Longrightarrow\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{9}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{27}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ | $\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{27}}\\sin{\\left(9 x + \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x &= {\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}1\\sin(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}\\sin(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{9}\\big|_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}} \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{18}-(- \\frac{1}{18}) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482724 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186482720 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482724 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [1759